osed_at":"2021-11-05T20:35:00Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\r\n\r\nAfter upgrading SQLAlchemy from 1.2.19 to latest, I got this error from a query which used to work.\r\n\r\nIt seems like SQLAlchemy may be generating an incorrect query in this case `IN (8, <uuid>)` instead of `IN ((8, <uuid>))`.\r\n\r\n\r\n### To Reproduce\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndb_session.query(LinkedProfile).filter(\r\n    LinkedProfile.parent == self,\r\n    tuple_(LinkedProfile.role_id, LinkedProfile.child_id).in_(deleted_links)\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere, `deleted_links` is a set of pairs like `{(8, UUID(...))}`.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Error\r\n\r\n```\r\nsqlalchemy.exc.OperationalError: (pymysql.err.OperationalError) (1241, 'Operand should contain 2 column(s)')\r\n[SQL: \r\n\r\nSELECT\r\n\tlinked_profile.role_id AS linked_profile_role_id,\r\n\tlinked_profile.parent_id AS linked_profile_parent_id,\r\n\tlinked_profile.child_id AS linked_profile_child_id,\r\n\tenum_associated_role_1.id AS enum_associated_role_1_id,\r\n\tenum_associated_role_1.name AS enum_associated_role_1_name \r\nFROM linked_profile\r\n\tLEFT OUTER JOIN enum_associated_role AS enum_associated_role_1\r\n\tON enum_associated_role_1.id = linked_profile.role_id \r\nWHERE\r\n\t%(param_1)s = linked_profile.parent_id AND\r\n\t(linked_profile.role_id, linked_profile.child_id) IN (%(param_2_1)s)\r\n[parameters: {'param_1': b'\\x9b{\"\\xdb\\x9cTFi\\x80\\x12\\xe2:\\x80\\xca\\x8f\\xb4', 'param_2_1': (8, UUID('9eeb5951-e25f-4879-9147-2237ee9d10d2'))}]\r\n``` \r\n\r\n### Versions\r\n\r\n- OS: linux\r\n- Python: 3.6\r\n- SQLAlchemy: latest published version\r\n- Database: MySQL\r\n- DBAPI (eg: psycopg, cx_oracle, mysqlclient): pymysql\r\n\r\n\r\n### Additional context\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7292/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7292/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}